  "Since its founding in 1851, _The New York Times_ has endorsed a candidate for president of the United States in every election in the paper's history.",
  "The first endorsement was in 1852 for Winfield Scott, and the most recent one was for Kamala Harris in 2024.",
  "Its first seven endorsements after Scott were for Republicans, and it was not until 1884 that it backed its first Democrat, Grover Cleveland.",
  "In total it has endorsed the Democratic candidate twenty nine times, the Republican thirteen times (the last being Dwight D.",
  "Eisenhower in 1956), a Whig candidate once (Winfield Scott in 1852), and a third-party candidate once (John M.",
  "Palmer in 1896).",
